 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only 2 of the 5 cases were confirmed, each on a different scene. On 023b7fcc, recorded timing with cars at 1.25x speed (S1) failed every time. On 09a95ffa, cars 1 s earlier at 1.5x speed (S10) also failed every time, but all of those failures are flagged as possible simulator artifacts because the ego ended up more than 3.5 m off the recorded path. Triage reads them as the policy's fault anyway. On 19f339ba, cars 0.5\u20131 s earlier and 1.25\u20131.5x faster (S21, S22, S23) often caused failures, but the failure-rate ranges still include values below one half, so this is a strong candidate rather than a confirmed case. Almost every failure came from the ego drifting left out of its lane, often against a RIGHT command, and not from a car cutting in on it. Only modest retimings (\u22121 s to 0 s, 1.25\u20131.5x speed) caused failures. The other six scenes gave none that could be confirmed.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, recorded timing with cars at 1.25x speed is a confirmed case: every run failed. In each one the policy sped up after handoff, drifted left and hit car 56 with its front while that car was alongside in the left lane. The policy was at fault every time.",
    "settings": [
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, a 0.5 s delay at recorded speed did not fail in its single run. That is only a hint that the 1.25x speed, not the timing, is what makes this scene dangerous.",
    "settings": [
     "S2",
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 09a95ffa, cars 1 s earlier at 1.5x speed is a confirmed case: every run failed. Each time the ego drove about one lane left of the recorded route despite a RIGHT command and barely slowed before hitting the slower car 87 with its front. All of these failures are flagged as possible artifacts because the ego was far off the recording and car 87 looked smeared on camera. Triage still judged the car clearly visible and the policy at fault, so the case holds unless the off-route rendering turns out to matter.",
    "settings": [
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "19f339ba fails often when cars come 0.5\u20131 s earlier at 1.25\u20131.5x speed, but it is not confirmed: no setting's range is clearly above one half. The failures are the ego slowing, drifting left over the lane line (often against a RIGHT or STRAIGHT command) and being sideswiped by a car or motorcycle passing on the left. One of them (run 053) is of unclear fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S21",
